# Files the Vercel CLI must not upload (npm run deploy). Secrets stay local;
# Vercel installs dependencies and builds itself.
#
# Patterns follow .gitignore rules: a name WITHOUT a leading slash matches at
# any depth. Anchor every project-root folder with "/" so a route folder with
# the same name is still deployed (QA-002: an unanchored `uploads` dropped
# app/api/vendor/media/uploads/, so photo uploads 405'd on live).
# tests/qa1-vendor.test.mjs checks that no pattern here excludes a source file.
.env*
!.env.example
!.env.deploy.example
node_modules
/uploads
/.next
/.next-*
/test-results*
/playwright-report
/tests
/e2e
/skills-lock.json
/.claude
/.agents
*.tsbuildinfo
